▸ PDF quality is sticky: `save as … file format format PDF` inherits whatever 
'Optimize for' you last chose in Word's own Save As dialog.
  Open any document in Word once, File > Save As > PDF, and pick the SECOND 
option, Best for printing.
  That choice persists; this script cannot set it. Pass --no-check-preset to 
stop seeing this.
▸ A redline PDF shows tracked changes the way Word is currently set to show them
(Review ▸ Markup display, and Print Markup).
  Open one redline in Word by hand and confirm it looks right before running the
batch — this script cannot set that for you.
